USC: exact 8 and 16-bit integer division

OpenCL's x / y and x % y on uchar and ushort (and their vectors) reach USC
as a DIV or DIV2 in U8_UN or U16.  U8_UN went to ExpandFloatDIV, which made
a UFOP_RECIP in U8_UN that nothing converts (icvt_i32.c: imgabort), and the
16-bit expansion multiplies by the floating point reciprocal and truncates,
so an exact quotient whose reciprocal rounds down comes out one too small.
Both widen to 32 bits and use the 32-bit integer divide.

